<title>PORTUGAL: PORTUGAL PUBLIC SECTOR WAGE TALKS DUE IN SEPTEMBER.</title>
<headline>PORTUGAL PUBLIC SECTOR WAGE TALKS DUE IN SEPTEMBER.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government and public sector unions will begin 1998 wage talks on September 24, a senior government official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But Under-Secretary of State for Public Administration Fausto Correia declined to comment on what the government's offer would be.</p>
<p>For 1997, the two sides agreed on three-percent wage rises against the government's 2.5-percent inflation target for the year.</p>
<p>The government is forecasting inflation, as measured by a rolling 12-month average, should slow to 2.3 percent next year.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
